WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:09.540
A bullet flies at four hundred meters per second. You can see it. You can count every spin. And for the first time in your life... seeing it isn't enough.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:20.120
Three days earlier, you got into a black car with a man you'd never met. Which, to be fair, your mom told you never to do.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.840
So... where are we going?

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.160
Somewhere that doesn't exist.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:34.360
There are eight billion people on this planet. Eleven of them are as fast as you. We find them. We test them.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.420
And then what?

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.860
That depends on whether they pass.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.470
And waiting inside... was someone you knew.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.980
Doctor Lee? You told them about me?

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.990
I told them the truth, Max. Your brain is... unusual.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:59.600
Test one: the light board. Buttons light up at random. Most people hit about one a second. You hit them before they finish lighting up.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:09.940
Test two: a tennis serve at two hundred and fifty kilometers per hour. Normal players guess where it's going. You just... watch.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.690
So you're the goalkeeper who threw away the World Cup. Cute.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.790
And you are?

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:27.400
Number six. Six times faster than normal. And, until today... the fastest person in this building.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.980
Test three: twenty drones, programmed to hit you. By the time the computer decides where to fly... you've already moved.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:41.870
Show-off.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.830
His numbers are better than three days ago.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:46.830
Better how?

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:47.980
Faster.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.040
Rubber rounds. It'll sting. Try not to get hit.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:06.740
Back to the bullet. A pistol round covers twenty meters in about one twentieth of a second. Your brain sees it in a fortieth. Plenty of time.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:21.380
Except... your brain is ten times faster. Your body isn't. To dodge it, you'd have to move your whole head in a few hundredths of a second. No human muscle can do that. Not even yours.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.610
Ow. Okay. That's... not fair.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:36.500
Everybody tries to beat the bullet. That's why everybody gets hit. Stop watching the bullet. Watch the trigger.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:48.300
Because before any gun fires, a finger has to squeeze. A shoulder tenses. An eye narrows. To everyone else, it's one moment. To you... it's a warning.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.200
So you don't dodge the bullet. You dodge the decision.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.060
Okay. That one was cool.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.100
But every time you did it... the headache came back. A little stronger.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:17.260
At three hundred kilometers per hour, a normal driver travels seventeen meters before they even notice the crash ahead. You? Two.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:29.100
Two fighter jets flying straight at each other close a kilometer every second. Pilots train for years to survive that. You just... had time.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.400
They're going to put you in everything. Jets, cars, whatever's faster.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:37.700
And you?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.490
They stopped putting me in things after year two.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:48.920
There's a cost. A faster brain burns more fuel. You were hungry all the time.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.440
That's your eighth burger.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.360
It's my brain's eighth burger.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.670
And there was something nobody told you.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.450
Max... how are the headaches?

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.210
Fine. Why?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:03.700
No reason.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:15.120
The final exam. No machines. No drones. Just one opponent. And nobody would tell you who.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.840
Nobody's ever finished this test.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:27.920
Every move you made, he'd already seen. Every move he made, you saw coming. For the first time in your life... someone was moving at your speed.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.450
And then... he got faster.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.300
That's... impossible.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.850
I was the first. Twenty years ago. Twenty times faster than normal.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.490
Then why do you need me?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.670
Because it's burning me out.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.960
The man who'd been testing you for days... was the one who needed help.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.250
Then we find a way to stop it. For both of us.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.100
It's not stopping. Every day, he's faster.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.640
Mine stopped at twenty. And then it started taking things back.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.420
And if his doesn't stop?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.920
Then one day, he'll look at the world... and it won't be moving at all.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.490
That night, your best friend called. For you, the ring took almost three seconds.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.630
Dude, where are you? You've been gone three days.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.510
Jake... how long does a second feel to you?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.080
What? Like... a second?

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:40.910
They told you it's a gift, right? They told me that too.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.790
What happened to number five?

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:46.740
He was my brother.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.610
His brain kept getting faster... until one day, he just stopped answering.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:58.970
Ten times faster today. Eleven tomorrow. And nobody knows where it ends.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:13.870
But is any of this real? In sprinting, a start faster than one tenth of a second counts as a false start, because no human is believed to react that fast. Formula One drivers react in about two tenths.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:27.880
But some animals already live in slow motion. A fly sees about two hundred and fifty images every second. We see about sixty. To a fly, your hand moves in slow motion... which is why it's so hard to swat one.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.830
So in a way, flies already live in Max's world.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:43.560
So... could a brain really keep getting faster, forever? What do you think? Tell us in the comments. And if you want Part 3... hit like, and subscribe so you don't miss it.

